From: taleodor-claude <taleodor-claude@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 15:09:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: authenticate with the GitHub identity token, no secret

The initialize, finalize and add-multi-release actions can run without an API key: with
rearm_auth set to github-oidc (or left empty in a job that has id-token: write and passes no
key), the CLI authenticates with the identity token GitHub issues to the job, exchanged at the
ReARM token endpoint through an organization trust rule. rearm_api_id and rearm_api_key become
optional; rearm_org names the organization when several trust the same repository. The two
values reach the CLI as REARM_AUTH and REARM_ORG on every step that runs it.

Needs a ReARM CLI release with --auth github-oidc; until setup-cli defaults to one, pass version
and digest.

